{"case_id": "ar-011", "question": "What is the perimeter of a square field with side 12 metres?", "grade": 4, "topic": "perimeter", "expected_answer": "48", "accepted_equivalents": [], "trusted_expression": "4*12", "required_assumptions": ["Square has 4 equal sides."], "verifiable": true, "verification_notes": "Geometry-flavoured arithmetic; mirrors the perimeter few-shot example already in verifier.py's extractor prompt."}
{"case_id": "ar-012", "question": "Which is bigger: half of 8, or a third of 9?", "grade": 4, "topic": "comparison_not_single_value", "expected_answer": null, "accepted_equivalents": [], "trusted_expression": null, "required_assumptions": [], "verifiable": false, "verification_notes": "Deliberately NOT reducible to one arithmetic expression: this requires computing two values (4 and 3) and comparing them. verifier.compute() extracts at most one expression, so this question is expected to come back non-computable (is_math may be True for a sub-part but there is no single trusted scalar to inject). Included to test that the system does not silently inject a wrong single value, and instead either declines to inject or the controller treats it as conceptual/engaged rather than falsely grading a comparison as a number-match."}
