{"case_id": "ar-018", "question": "What is the HCF (highest common factor) of 12 and 18?", "grade": 5, "topic": "hcf", "expected_answer": "6", "accepted_equivalents": ["HCF 6", "GCF 6"], "trusted_expression": null, "required_assumptions": ["HCF/GCD is outside scripts.llm.verifier's current arithmetic grammar (+,-,*,/,**,parens only), so trusted_expression is null here. The expected answer was independently checked with sympy.gcd(12, 18) in this authoring pass (result: 6), NOT through the production verifier path -- a future extraction/verifier extension would be needed before this case can be auto-scored end-to-end."], "verifiable": true, "verification_notes": "Fills the single largest confirmed curriculum gap identified in docs/curriculum_coverage_matrix.md: Class 5 'Factors & Multiples' had zero evaluation items despite confirmed corpus support (grade-5 corpus matches for factor/multiple/HCF/LCM terms, e.g. page 6)."}
